WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.850
I know where your sister is.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.100
How could you lie to me?!

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.690
This is why you were blacklisted by 
the FSC and lost your regular spot!

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.970
So-chan, sorry.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:14.740
If that's the case, I'm sure
 Sogo will understand.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.370
Sogo-san?

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.790
How is he doing?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.310
He's stable now. Riku-san is with him.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.920
Riku-san also showed me 
what to do at the hospital.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.760
Nanase-san did say he spent 
a lot of time staying in hospitals.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.580
Why did they say he collapsed?

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.970
Acute gastritis caused by stress.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.680
Oh, stress.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.230
I'm sorry.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.530
It's my fault.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.460
I put too much responsibility on Sogo-san.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.520
No!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.640
It's my fault So-chan collapsed.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.920
Tamaki.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.140
It's because of all the trouble I caused him.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.280
It's my fault.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.970
He should've told us he needed help.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.860
We're friends, after all.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.940
You guys have a minute?

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.960
Sogo-san says he wants to tell us something.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.140
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.680
Someday we'll make it past there

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.110
We don't know what's right

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.320
So we Try and Jump!

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.490
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.120
For us It's Only Way!

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.290
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.300
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.470
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:58.300
Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.720
In the light!

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.510
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:08.970
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.770
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.280
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:21.780
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:28.750
The future surely lies on the other side

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.670
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.050
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:41.300
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.020
#13 What Was Lost

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.980
Sorry, guys.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.940
And Manager, sorry for making you worry.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.680
It's not—

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.770
Sorry, So-chan!

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.860
It's my fault you collapsed!

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.110
Tamaki-kun.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.130
Seriously, sorry!

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.870
I'm really sorry!

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:14.170
I asked you all here so
 I could tell you something.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.470
I might quit.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.370
You mean quit MEZZO"?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.080
Not just MEZZO".

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.310
IDOLiSH7, too.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:27.790
You can't.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.770
Why?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.550
Did you really hate it that much?

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:33.270
Huh?

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.620
Then you should've told me!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.240
I told you to tell me!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.530
I'm stupid, so I won't 
know unless you tell me!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:43.500
Stop, Tama!

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.020
He's sick!

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:49.260
How could you make this
decision on your own?!

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.290
What are you talking about?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.260
The reason you're quitting!

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.360
You're quitting 'cause 
you're mad at me, right?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.170
I never said that!

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.090
But what else could it be?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.510
When you collapsed and they 
took you away in the ambulance,

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:13.270
I swore that I'd never bother you again...

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.980
And now it's over?

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.980
Tamaki-kun.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:22.230
So, listen to Tama.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.390
Won't you reconsider?

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:29.350
Yeah. Just hit him a couple 
times and make up.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.310
He's really sorry about what he did.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.330
In his own way.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.040
Yes. Please.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:43.330
It's true that I did have some issues 
with Tamaki-kun, but that's not why.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:49.570
I heard our namesake show was canceled 
because of our sponsor, the FSC.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.070
What about it?

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.930
It's my fault.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:05:00.150
The chairman of the FSC Group 
is my father, Osaka Soshi.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.150
Seriously?!

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.910
The FSC?

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.500
The Five Star Company is one of 
Japan's most iconic corporations.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.430
Yes. They're internationally famous.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.450
And you're... his son?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:15.270
I knew you were from a good family.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.720
But how is that your fault?

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.750
Wouldn't your dad support you?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.920
My father is opposed to my 
working in the music industry.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.060
When President Takanashi 
scouted me, he was against it.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.350
But I couldn't give up music.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.310
I dropped out of college to join the agency.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.940
He disowned me then, though.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.940
So that's what you meant 
by abandoning your family.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:50.420
Why did you want to pursue music?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.750
My uncle was a musician.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:58.330
He wasn't very popular, but he'd always 
happily tell me about his band.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.530
I loved my uncle and his music.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:06.340
But like me, the family 
disapproved and disowned him.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.970
He fell ill and died.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.930
At my uncle's funeral...

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:15.390
It was hard hearing everyone 
saying, "I told you so."

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.240
"I told you so."

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.850
This happened because he'd spent all his 
energy on something as unreliable as music.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.820
"I told you so."

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.440
He would've been happy if he'd pursued 
a stable life instead of a silly dream.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.190
"I told you so."

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.040
But I...

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.330
Thought they were wrong?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.410
Yeah.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.170
After all, my uncle was happy.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.170
He had a wonderful life.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:46.000
I entered this world because I wanted 
to shout at them that they were wrong.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:48.970
I see.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.010
You finally told us about yourself.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.970
It's not very interesting.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.140
I didn't think you'd care.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.650
No, it's nothing like that!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:02.050
You and your uncle are right.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.710
Music, dance.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.590
They're magic that make people happy.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.950
You're carrying on your uncle's will.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.790
Thanks.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.340
But if I stay, I'd only cause more trouble.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:18.270
The FSC has several partner companies.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:22.340
My father's influence would be behind 
every commercial on one of our shows.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.770
It would be better if I—

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.210
It's all right.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.770
We just have to become popular enough 
that we're beyond your dad's reach.

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:31.220
What?

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.390
You've heard of legendary idol Zero, right?

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.380
Zero's concerts couldn't be canceled.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:41.770
Not by the prime minister, not by the 
president, not by anyone in the world.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.180
We just have to become huge stars.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:48.400
We just have to get so big, we can
 blow everyone out of our way.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:49.690
But...

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:54.220
I predict we'll continue to 
receive offers for regular shows.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:58.690
Even for the FSC, it would be difficult 
to block us from everything.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.400
Sogo-san, don't worry.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.650
Someday... Someday your 
father will accept you.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:06.710
And your uncle.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.210
So...

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.690
It's okay if I stay?

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.760
As if you even need to ask.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:14.760
Ow!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.690
Take it easy today.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:20.020
We can start working again tomorrow.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.230
Thanks, everyone.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.020
Guys...

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.700
You'll damage your eyesight.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.390
If we're going to watch something,

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.160
let's watch the complete 
<i>MagiCona</i> box set all night.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.620
Don't drag anyone else down with you!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.580
Sorry...

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.000
Thanks.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.090
Yamato-san, please.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:57.780
I...

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:03.020
I feel like So-chan and I are a real duo now.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.210
That's great.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.490
Sogo didn't get a hole in 
his stomach for nothing.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:09.820
I'm glad we got to hear his SOS.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.390
It's a tall hurdle, but we have to try.

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.780
Yes. To become unbeatable idols.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.100
Yeah. Like Zero.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.100
<i>Taking Taking Taking!</i>

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:21.430
<i>Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:24.250
<i>(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.980
First, we need to catch up to them.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.640
<i>(Oi! Oi!) It's gotta be My way!</i>

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.580
TRIGGER...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.580
We still owe them for that song.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:30.330
<i>(Oi! Oi!) Let's do SUMMER!</i>

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:33.430
We're supposed to perform with them at 
<i>Sound Ship</i>, our next live broadcast concert.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.820
<i>(Oi! Oi!) How exciting!</i>

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.380
The blazing sun and sky

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.380
Our first time since the <i>Music Festa</i>, huh?

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:39.220
Lights our curiosity ablaze

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:39.220
This time we'll show 
Tenn-nii how strong we are.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.220
(So!) A mermaid waits by the shore

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.500
Thank you for your continued support.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:49.210
Excuse me.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.700
It's okay.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:53.900
We'll get another chance.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.070
Huh? You're from Takanashi Agency.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.100
Mr. Shimooka.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.900
Ah, it is you.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.270
Hello.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:04.060
I'm terribly sorry about the Music Festa.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.530
Don't worry about it!

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:09.830
Anyway, IDOLiSH7's been doing well lately.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.950
Thank you.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:14.460
I have a new variety show coming up.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.970
If I7 doesn't mind, why don't 
they come on as regular guests?

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:19.720
What?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.560
When I was a young man,

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:27.700
I got on a show through one of my
 seniors, and I completely bombed it.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.730
It makes me want to support you guys.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.610
Through your senior?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.110
What's this cake for?

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.820
<b>Congratulations on Rank 1</b>

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.820
<b>Let's Do Summer</b>

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.030
It's from the record company.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.620
Really? Can I eat just the strawberries?

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.890
Rude.

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:43.700
Better than leaving it untouched.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:48.750
Hey.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.140
Are you glad we ranked first with that song?

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.580
I like it.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:57.260
I was embarrassed at first since 
it's different from our usual songs.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.260
Don't you think it's similar 
to IDOLiSH7's songs?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.710
Theirs?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.640
Now that you mention it...

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.350
Come to think of it, I heard their 
center is your twin brother.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.600
He is?

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.450
He wanted to talk to you.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.100
He wanted to know why you 
abandoned your family.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.150
I don't know what you mean.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:20.020
Kujo Tenn, you were Nanase Tenn once.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:24.410
When you joined our agency, my father 
was actually excited for once.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.860
He said, "Kujo-san gave 
us an outstanding talent."

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:30.190
Who's Kujo-san?

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:34.920
Gaku, we're business partners, not friends.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.590
I have no intention of telling 
you about my personal life.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.690
Why, you...

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.190
Knock it off, guys.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.330
Come in.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.010
E-Excuse me.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:46.810
You're...

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:47.820
You know her?

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.730
She's IDOLiSH7's manager.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.130
Oh.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:59.320
I heard IDOLiSH7 appeared on <i>Music Festa</i>
 at Yaotome-san's recommendation.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.240
I'm sorry we haven't even 
thanked you until now.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.160
Is this true?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.580
I dunno.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.890
What? But...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.510
Anyway, want some cake?

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:11.310
Huh?!

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:14.040
Tenn will be angry if we don't eat it.

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.040
Uh, I...

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.540
Don't make her eat it.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.960
Girls like sweet things, right?

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.340
Right?

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.570
What?

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.850
Thanks for the cake...

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:25.890
Eat up.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:29.970
Hey.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.100
Why didn't you release a new song?

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.100
Huh?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.540
Your debut single.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.650
That was an existing song. Why?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.190
Now that you mention it...

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.390
Uh, because...

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:45.950
Th-There was a reason for that.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:48.070
Oh?

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.370
IDOLiSH7 seems busy these days.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.010
I'm looking forward to seeing what they do.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:56.590
Thank you.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:00.730
Huh?!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.260
You have cream on your face.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.430
There. All good.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.850
Th-Th-Th-Th-Thank you!

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.150
The new artist award.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:15.940
Huh?

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.870
The Japan Idol Music Awards' 
new artist award.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:21.450
The one we won last year.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:22.780
You should win.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.280
What?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:28.470
If you do, I'll tell Riku 
what he wants to know.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.180
Tell him that.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:35.770
What?

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.540
Tenn-nii will tell me if we 
win the new artist award?

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:43.170
Yes. He didn't say what it was about, though.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.590
What award is this?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.260
It's the Japan Idol Music Awards—

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.020
Excuse me.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:51.680
Yes?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.150
You're IDOLiSH7's Izumi Iori-kun, right?

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.570
Will you shake my hand?

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.190
What?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.860
Uh, sure.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.570
I always watch your web show.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.950
I love the way you go after your elders.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:08.660
I wish I could give my boss
 a tongue-lashing, too.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:10.830
Why don't you, then?

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:11.950
You idiot!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.450
Thank you.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.640
He's actually a really cute guy.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:16.980
We take really good care of him.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.870
You're one to talk.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.510
Anyway, how did you know it was us?

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.630
Huh? Because of that.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.380
I recognized the one who's on the billboard.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.700
What is that?

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:31.430
Nagi?

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.730
Yes! It's me.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.670
Clara Lowell?

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.860
That's a well-established 
brand, popular among women!

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:44.320
It's a super famous foreign high-end brand.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.980
When did you do that?

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.040
Oh, I went on a date with 
Clara the other day.

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.280
A date?!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.010
It says the designer chose 
to use an obscure model.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.990
Do you know what this means?

00:14:55.990 --> 00:15:02.540
If you'd just gone through the agency, 
we could've charged a huge talent fee!

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:07.660
Oh, but involving money in your 
dates with ladies is not very smart.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.420
Oh?

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:10.340
Rokuya-san, this ad with your face on it

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.430
is going to be plastered 
all over women's magazines!

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:13.930
In other words...

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.510
I'm going to be popu—

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.890
It's a great time for us to promote IDOLiSH7!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:23.350
Have we gotten any big offers?

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:28.290
M-Mr. Shimooka asked us to appear 
as regular guests on a show.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:32.970
And... we got an offer for Yamato-san 
to star in a drama series.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:33.550
Huh?

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:34.490
What's the theme song?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.030
It doesn't say anything.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.450
Make sure we get it!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.120
Got it! I'm off to work!

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.500
Take your business cards! And a sample CD!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.410
I will!

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.130
Nagi-san.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.510
Good job!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.750
Really?

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:52.130
Then it was worth the effort.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:58.830
Rokuya-san, next time make sure you 
get permission from the agency first.

00:15:58.830 --> 00:15:59.910
I see.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.900
Well, thanks to you, we have 
a chance to increase our notoriety.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:07.440
Then maybe we could win this 
something-or-other new artist award.

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.360
The Japan Idol Music Awards.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.860
What kind of contest is it?

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.360
Oh, right. You don't know what it is.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:18.890
The Japan Idol Music Awards, 
or JIMA for short.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.550
Impartially determined by CD sales,

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:26.450
it's the most influential music 
awards for Japanese idols.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:28.630
Great. That's amazing.

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:32.890
Winning the new artist award 
will nominate us for

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:35.720
the <i>Black or White Music Fantasia </i>
held every year on New Year's Eve.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:41.600
Last year's winners and this year's newbies 
from all musical genres battle onstage.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.300
If we were on it, we'd appear 
in the male idol category.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.420
And last year's winners were...

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:48.900
TRIGGER.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.090
If we win the new artist 
award at this year's JIMA,

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.240
we'll earn the right to compete against them.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:58.240
Not only that, but on the ultimate 
stage of the <i>Black or White</i> concert.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.020
Facing off against TRIGGER 
at the <i>Black or White</i>...

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.620
Hey, Iori. Is it impossible for us 
to win the new artist award?

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.380
No, it's possible.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.700
As long as you show your 
true strength to the media.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:16.290
You're never in top form 
when we're recording.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.700
Do you get nervous?

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.800
Well...

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:22.970
Usually fans aren't allowed in 
during recordings for music shows.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.070
It feels different from our concerts.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:28.820
Only the staff is there, so 
it really feels like a job.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:30.950
So it stunts your performance?

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:34.710
I can see how performing for 
fans would hype you up more.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.250
But I'll do my best.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:42.370
If we win the new artist award, 
we can compete against TRIGGER.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:45.360
Then Tenn-nii will talk to me.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.000
I want that new artist award.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:52.670
Then we need more people to 
know about our songs and us.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:57.780
Yes. As long as we keep gaining fame, 
we may actually be able to win the award.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.790
Why?

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.150
Why did it have to be you, too?

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.030
Yamato-kun's amazing.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.370
I heard he's starring in a drama.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.050
Really? What's it called?

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.120
Nikaido Yamato

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.120
Nemesis

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.120
<b>TV Watch</b>

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.120
<b>IDOLiSH7 
</b>Interview & Gravure
Present included!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.120
New Idol Collection Part 3

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:24.460
A sci-fi suspense show called <i>Nemesis</i>.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.570
It's about revenge, and 
there's even a love story.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:28.620
It's so cool!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.960
<b>TV Watch</b>

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.960
<b>IDOLiSH7
</b> Interview & Gravure
Present Included!

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.960
I7's been getting more exposure lately.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.710
They're going to be regular 
guests on a variety show.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.170
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:36.160
IDOLiSH7 to appear as regular guests on new 
"Mr. Shimooka's The TV Man Show!"

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.680
Wanna go see it together?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.100
Is this the show I7's on?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.180
<b>TV Watch</b>

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.180
<b>IDOLiSH7
</b>Interview & Gravure
 Present included!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.180
<b>New show starting!</b>

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.180
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:42.180
Yeah, that's it!

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.790
Mr. Shimooka's show!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.000
Wait, isn't that crazy?

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.410
I7 is insane.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:48.980
So insane. You have to watch it!

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:54.030
We got the theme song for the drama series!

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.160
Yeah!

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.610
Nicely done, Manager!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.320
I ordered delivery for lunch to celebrate.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.300
What?

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.370
Sounds like it's here.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.390
Thanks for your order.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.040
This is Yamamura Soba.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.920
Right here, please.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.750
Ten tempura sobas.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.930
They're hot.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.750
Wow, tsukimi soba?

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.230
It's tempura soba.

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:17.800
Wow. We can have this?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.470
Tempura, huh? Looks good.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:23.020
We're starting to get popular, aren't we?

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.020
It's hot!

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:24.800
Here's the money.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:26.260
<b>Soba Shop 
Yamamura</b>

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:26.260
Oh, thanks.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.640
T-TRIGGER's Yaotome Gaku-san?

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:34.190
I get that a lot, but I'm not him.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:35.950
I'm not that handsome.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:38.660
Sorry. You look just like him.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.910
Well, see you next time!

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.430
He really did look just like him.

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:50.660
But there's no way he works at a soba shop.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.170
<b>Soba Shop
Yamamura</b>

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:59.050
It's starting.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:19:59.930
Oh, no.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.170
Wait!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:17.340
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:13.180
Delivering energy to all of Japan, <i>Mr. 
Shimooka's The TV Man Show</i> starts now!

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:17.610
And here are my assistants, 
the members of IDOLiSH7!

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.570
Thank you for having us!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.540
You guys sure are popular.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:26.560
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.570
You're unstoppable right now.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.100
Not at all.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:28.830
Thank you.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.750
Yamato-kun, I heard you're 
starring in a drama.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:36.500
Nemesis

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:35.440
How cool, you look great!

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:36.500
Really?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.620
And you're singing the theme song?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.150
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.690
Dramas, modeling, variety shows...

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.780
Nice. You guys are busy.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:47.180
We've had our share of troubles, though.

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:49.490
That's fine!

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:52.070
It's better to make mistakes 
when you're young.

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:53.180
Thank you.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:21:00.410
Anyway, IDOLiSH7 will also be
 appearing on <i>Sound Ship</i>!

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.240
<b>Appearance scheduled!!</b>

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.780
Thank you!

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:07.160
We've received a request from our fans.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:12.370
"IDOLiSH7 sometimes holds hands and 
raises them during their concerts,

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.860
but Riku-kun and Iori-kun 
haven't done it yet."

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:18.470
"Could you please do it at Sound Ship?"

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:19.630
Hear that?

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:20.630
We won't.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.490
Not with Iori.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:24.700
But your fans want to see it.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.050
They also say when Nagi-kun 
and Mitsuki-kun do it,

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.890
it looks like Mitsuki-kun's being lifted up.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:33.690
Hooray!

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.400
Like an alien being arreste—

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:36.690
Hey, shut up!

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.490
Does MEZZO" do it?

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.470
We're not that kind of group.

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:43.050
We keep things dry.

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:43.610
I know!

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.070
We'll do it if MEZZO" does it!

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:46.990
You can't just decide that!

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.760
I already heard it.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:50.290
You can't take it back.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:51.120
What?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.830
I guess the rest of us will 
do the alien being arrested.

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:54.830
Promise me you won't do it.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.340
What?

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.380
Sure. Let's do it!

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:58.790
Don't call me an alien!

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:05.290
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:04.710
Finally, could you tell us 
your hopes for <i>Sound Ship</i>?

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:05.300
Sure.

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:07.130
At <i>Sound Ship</i>,

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:12.260
we hope to perform at full power for 
the fans in the audience and at home.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:14.850
We appreciate your support.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.310
Good luck with this show and everything else!

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.730
Thanks!

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.730
Yes!

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.950
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:44.960
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:58.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.270
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:08.360
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:13.490
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:16.040
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:18.580
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.460
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:26.380
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:42.530
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.530 --> 00:23:46.900
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:51.260
Seek now?
